  "question": {
    "text": "A bi convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is cut in two identical parts along a plane perpendicular to the principal axis. The power of each lens after cut is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The focal&nbsp;length of the bi-convex lens&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>f</mi></mfenced></math> can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>(</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>When the lens is cut into two halves, the focal length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of each part can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>(</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8734;</mo></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio of the powers for both the lenses can be&nbsp;given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Substitute the value of the known parameter into equation (3) to calculate the required power.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}